//==
// # Host interop root
//
// The compiler-assumed primitives that used to live here (Number, Integer, Boolean,
// String, Character, Dynamic) moved to `primitives.plato` and are now declared with
// the `primitive` keyword (plato-367). What remains is the one type in this family
// that is NOT a primitive: the compiler does not assume `Object` by name, and it is
// not on the writer primitive list, so its declaration is its own authority.

// The root reference type for interop with host platforms.
type Object
{ }
